<title>PERU: Peru August molybdenum output rises 45.6 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru August molybdenum output rises 45.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's molybdenum output rose 45.6 percent to 351 tonnes in August, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Friday.</p>
<p>Production rose 0.4 percent to 2,119 tonnes in the first eight months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Molybdenum output rose 19.5 percent to 3,411 tonnes in 1995 compared with 2,854 tonnes during the previous year.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Southern Peru Ltd is Peru's main producer of molybdenum.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
